---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Francesca Bucci"
  description="About Francesca Bucci, a data protection professional writing on digital privacy."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">About</span>
      <h1>I work in privacy.<br /><em>I write to understand it.</em></h1>
      <p>Practitioner notes from someone who's been inside the machine long enough to know where it squeaks.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="prose-page">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <p>
        I'm Francesca Bucci. I work as a data protection professional at a
        technology company, where my days are spent running DPIAs, untangling
        vendor data-processing agreements, sitting in on product reviews, and
        trying to make privacy something engineers want to build for — not a
        form they fill in at the end.
      </p>

      <p>
        Before going in-house, I spent time on the consultancy side, advising
        clients across SaaS, healthtech, and adtech on GDPR compliance, transfer
        mechanisms, and the unglamorous mechanics of records of processing. I
        hold the <strong>CIPP/E</strong> and <strong>CIPM</strong> certifications
        from the IAPP.
      </p>

      <h2>Why I write</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy is a field where the rules change faster than the practice, and
        the practice changes faster than the culture. I started this blog
        because I kept finding that the most useful things I knew — the
        specific, unglamorous lessons from real DPIAs, real vendor reviews,
        real conversations with engineers — weren't written down anywhere.
      </p>

      <p>
        So this is where I write them down. Mostly for myself, to think
        clearly. But also for the other practitioners, engineers, founders, and
        curious readers who keep showing up in my inbox with the same
        questions. If that's you, hi.
      </p>

      <h2>What I cover</h2>
      <p>
        I write about the things I'm actually working on: GDPR in practice
        (not the textbook version), the EU AI Act as it starts to bite,
        privacy engineering as a discipline, the politics and mechanics of
        international data transfers, and the new frontiers — large language
        models, federated learning, biometric inference — where the old
        playbook is starting to crack.
      </p>

      <h2>What this isn't</h2>
      <p>
        This isn't legal advice. I'm not a lawyer, and even if I were, the
        answer to almost every privacy question is "it depends." Treat this as
        one practitioner's notes, not as a substitute for advice tailored to
        your situation.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        If you want to talk about a privacy question, a project, or just
        compare notes, the inbox is open:
        <a href="mailto:Francesca@example.com">Francesca@example.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
